<title>HUNGARY: FORECAST - Hungary's T-bill yields seen falling.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Hungary's T-bill yields seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's discount Treasury bill average yields are expected to continue their falling trend at this week's auctions, traders said.</p>
<p>The Government Debt Management Agency (AAKK) will hold a one-month Treasury bill auction on Tuesday, a three-month one on Wednesday, a six-month auction on Thursday and a 12-month auction on Friday. </p>
<p>			    1-MONTH    3-MONTH    6-MONTH 12-MONTH</p>
<p>				HTBM	HTBN	HTBO	 HTBP</p>
<p>Amount on offer</p>
<p>  (bln forints)	    1	    5	   14	    14</p>
<p>Previous average(pct)   22.84	22.80	23.53	 23.69</p>
<p>Valid bid range(pct)    +1/-2    +0.5/-2    +0.5/-2     +0.5/-2</p>
<p>FORECAST OF HUNGARIAN TRADERS Zsolt Bango/Gog Securities</p>
<p>    AVERAGE		 22.80	22.60	22.82	 23.03</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM		 23.00	22.65	22.90	 23.05</p>
<p>Balint Bozo/Postabank Securities</p>
<p>    AVERAGE		 22.50	22.55	22.85	 22.90</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM		 22.60	22.65	22.90	 22.99</p>
<p>-- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410</p>
